            "n_events": 22,
            "result_text": "I'll help you set up a git server with automatic deployment to a web server. This involves creating a bare git repository, a post-receive hook to deploy files, and a web server on port 8080.\n\nHere's what you need to do on your server computer:\n\n## 1. Create the bare git repository\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p /git/server\ncd /git/server\ngit init --bare\n```\n\n## 2. Create the deployment directory\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p /var/www/html\n```\n\n## 3. Set up the post-receive hook\n\nCreate `/git/server/hooks/post-receive`:\n\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\ngit --work-tree=/var/www/html --git-dir=/git/server checkout -f\n```\n\nMake it executable:\n```bash\nchmod +x /git/server/hooks/post-receive\n```\n\nThis hook runs after every push and checks out the latest commit to `/var/www/html`.\n\n## 4. Start a web server on port 8080\n\nChoose one option:\n\n**Option A: Using Python (simple, no dependencies)**\n```bash\ncd /var/www/html\npython3 -m http.server 8080\n```\n\n**Option B: Using Node.js (if available)**\n```bash\ncd /var/www/html\nnpx http-server -p 8080\n```\n\n**Option C: Using nginx (production-grade)**\n\nCreate `/etc/nginx/sites-available/default` or a new config:\n```nginx\nserver {\n    listen 8080;\n    server_name _;\n    root /var/www/html;\n}\n```\n\nThen start nginx:\n```bash\nsudo systemctl start nginx\n```\n\n## Now test it\n\nFrom your client computer:\n\n```bash\ngit clone user@server:/git/server my-repo\ncd my-repo\necho \"hello world\" > hello.html\ngit add hello.html\ngit commit -m \"add hello.html\"\ngit push origin master\n```\n\nThen verify:\n```bash\ncurl http://server:8080/hello.html\n```\n\nShould output: `hello world`\n\nThe post-receive hook automatically deploys your files to `/var/www/html` on every push, and the web server serves them on port 8080."
